<h1>Danielle Carter-Walters</h1>
<p>Co-founder of Chicago Flips Red. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>A conservative organizer, fitness trainer, and small business owner married to a retired Chicago police officer, running as a law-and-order outsider. Filed 13,000 signatures within an hour of the deadline.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.dannicformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (dannicformayor.com)</a></p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Only Carter-Walters: A Chicago DOGE office to audit city spending.</p>
<p>Not published: Nineteen issue headings on the site, each a slogan with no policy behind it yet.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>A Chicago DOGE accountability office to cut waste, expose fraud, and fund the basics. <q>Cut waste. Expose fraud. Fund the basics.</q> (<a href="https://www.dannicformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">dannicformayor.com</a>)</li>
<li>Restore law and order. <q>Restore law and order.</q> (<a href="https://www.dannicformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">dannicformayor.com</a>)</li>
<li>Stop what the campaign calls taxing the city into decline. <q>Stop taxing decline.</q> (<a href="https://www.dannicformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">dannicformayor.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<p>No spending report found for this campaign yet.</p>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC).</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would cut waste and expose fraud through a Chicago DOGE accountability office, and stop raising taxes on a shrinking city.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>Cut waste. Expose fraud. Fund the basics.</q> (<a href="https://www.dannicformayor.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">dannicformayor.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
